    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0257" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v02/pg227"/>

                <head>129. Letter From Secretary of State Herter to Foreign Minister Pella<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d129-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February 2,
                        1960</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Pella</hi>: I just wanted to send you this
                    personal note of appreciation for your very generous action with respect to the
                    presidency of the next General Assembly of the United Nations. When I talked to
                    Ambassador Brosio about this matter,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d129-f2"/> I tried to
                    make it very clear that I found myself in an extremely difficult position both
                    because I count you as a close personal friend and because of our great
                    friendship for your nation. However, under the circumstances, I know that we
                    both share the same concern lest we drift into the difficulty <pb facs="0258"
                        n="228" xml:id="pg228"/> which led to the impasse over the Security Council
                    seat last year and might even find a Communist elected to the presidency of the
                    General Assembly. Your own fine action has, I think, gone a long way toward
                    mitigating these dangers.</p>
                <p>With warmest personal regards,</p>
                <p>Most sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Christian A. Herter<anchor n="3"
                                xml:id="d129-f3"/></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
